  "types": [
    {
      "name": "ExpiryBook",
      "docs": [
        "How much of the reserve is committed to rounds that all settle at the same instant.",
        "",
        "The global exposure cap bounds the whole book, but it says nothing about *when* the book comes due. Without",
        "this, every open round could sit on one 15:00 boundary: one print would then decide the reserve's entire",
        "position, which is the concentration the per-expiry cap exists to prevent. Keyed by the boundary rather than",
        "by the Window, because two Series expiring together are one risk."
      ],
      "type": {
        "kind": "struct",
        "fields": [
          {
            "name": "reserve",
            "type": "pubkey"
          },
          {
            "name": "expiry_sec",
            "type": "i64"
          },
          {
            "name": "locked_base",
            "docs": [
              "Provider capital committed to open rounds settling at this boundary."
            ],
            "type": "u64"
          },
          {
            "name": "rounds_open",
            "type": "u64"
          },
          {
            "name": "bump",
            "type": "u8"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "ParamsUpdated",
      "type": {
        "kind": "struct",
        "fields": [
          {
            "name": "reserve",
            "type": "pubkey"
          },
          {
            "name": "paused",
            "type": "bool"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Provider",
      "docs": [
        "One liquidity provider's claim on the reserve.",
        "",
        "The reserve keeps `supply_shares` as the total, but a total cannot tell one provider from another: without a",
        "per-provider record there is nothing to check a withdrawal against, and the first caller could redeem the",
        "whole supply. Shares live here, one account per wallet, and only ever move through that wallet's own signature."
      ],
      "type": {
        "kind": "struct",
        "fields": [
          {
            "name": "reserve",
            "type": "pubkey"
          },
          {
            "name": "owner",
            "type": "pubkey"
          },
          {
            "name": "shares",
            "type": "u64"
          },
          {
            "name": "supplied_base",
            "docs": [
              "What this provider has put in and taken out, so a front end can show a return without replaying events."
            ],
            "type": "u64"
          },
          {
            "name": "withdrawn_base",
            "type": "u64"
          },
          {
            "name": "bump",
            "type": "u8"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "RangeParams",
      "docs": [
        "The reserve's tunables, mirrored by `RangeParams` in `packages/core/src/range/types.ts`."
      ],
      "type": {
        "kind": "struct",
        "fields": [
          {
            "name": "margin_bps",
            "docs": [
              "The reserve's edge over fair value, in basis points."
            ],
            "type": "u16"
          },
          {
            "name": "max_exposure_bps",
            "docs": [
